Socket plumbing shared by the `ca::sys` net wrappers, without system headers in any header.

- `sockaddr_ipv4` and `sockaddr_unix`: struct sockaddr_in and sockaddr_un as the platform lays
  them out, with `to_sockaddr` / `from_sockaddr` / `checked_endpoint` for `ipv4_endpoint` and
  `to_sockaddr(path, out)` for Unix paths (abstract names included); layouts checked against
  `<netinet/in.h>` and `<sys/un.h>` in the sibling `.cpp` files.
- `socket_constants`: `IPPROTO_TCP`, `TCP_NODELAY`, `SHUT_*`, `SOL_SOCKET` and the `SO_*`
  options ca sets, per platform, checked against the system headers.
- `open_socket(family, type, protocol, flags)`: socket() with the `fs::cloexec` / `fs::nonblock`
  flag check every socket constructor shares (atomic on Linux, fcntl elsewhere), and
  `discard_socket(fd)` for closing a socket after a failure that is returned instead.
